title: Runtime verification — R3 video provider paints; "caption stacking" was a 2-frame cross-fade artifact
summary: |-
  Drove the studio under headless Puppeteer (transient install in /tmp/verify-rig) from creator/ so workspace mode boots. Confirmed all R3 + R2 fixes at runtime via DOM evidence + canvas.toDataURL() snapshots: video paints inside the portrait 9:16 canvas (BrowserVideoFrameProvider works end-to-end with srcResolver → /api/file?path=… → 87MB MOV streaming with Range support); canvas-size dropdown intact (4 presets, "Portrait 9:16 — 1080×1920" selected); timeline ruler horizontal (8 ticks at 0/30/60/90/120/150/180/210, left styles 0px → 1334.75px); canvas letterbox-fits (1080×1920 raster, 468×832 CSS). Caption gating confirmed at frame 0 (only cap-0 "Just"), frame 86 (only cap-1 "recording a quic[k]"), frame 115 (only cap-2 "some au[dio]"), frame 200 (only cap-5 "."). KEY FINDING: scrubbed to frame 89 and CAPTURED THE CROSS-FADE — cap-1 (1→0) and cap-2 (0→1) over [88,90] both render at ~0.6846 opacity for 2 frames (66ms at 30fps), producing exactly the "stacked text" visual the owner reported. The doc data, resolver, and renderer were all correct then too; the owner just scrubbed into the 2-frame cross-fade window and assumed it was a renderer bug. Resolver math probe from earlier session was bulletproof; runtime now confirms it. Also caught a benign-but-wasteful issue: 5× net::ERR_ABORTED on the 87MB MOV during initial mount cascade — workspace-app's clearMain → currentStudio.destroy → canvas-panel.destroy → videoProvider.dispose calls video.removeAttribute('src') + load() mid-fetch each time. Video eventually loads on the final mount (proven by painted frames). Worth a v1.1 polish: defer provider.create() until first get() for a renderable video layer, or pool the video cache across AtelierStudio instances.</summary>
  <parameter name="symbols_touched">["#browser-video-frame-provider", "#canvas-panel", "#atelier-studio", "#workspace-app", "#timeline-view"]
learnings:
  - Cross-fade animations have a runtime-visible window — for a 2-frame cross-fade at 30fps that's only 66ms, but a scrubbed/paused screenshot at exactly that frame shows BOTH layers at ~0.68 opacity, looking visually identical to a 'multiple captions stacking simultaneously' bug. When investigating animation rendering bugs from static screenshots, account for the possibility of capturing a transition frame.
  - Detached HTMLVideoElement (created with document.createElement('video') but never appendChild'd) is a valid pattern for canvas frame sources via drawImage. document.querySelectorAll('video') WON'T find them — they're not in the live DOM tree. Look for them in the provider's internal Map instead.
  - Vite's /@fs/ path serves source files directly from disk — useful for verifying that a deep package's source has reached the browser without grepping the bundled output. curl http://localhost:PORT/@fs/<absolute-path> bypasses the bundler entirely.
  - video.removeAttribute('src') + video.load() during a dispose() aborts any in-flight HTTP fetch with net::ERR_ABORTED. Harmless for correctness (the next mount re-fetches and succeeds) but wasteful — for a 87MB file across 5 abort/retry cycles that's 435MB of unnecessary bandwidth on every initial doc load.
